+- `onError` fires for every rejection: an `Error` reaches the hook as the same instance, while any non-`Error` rejection — such as a string, a plain object, or `undefined` — is wrapped in an `Error` whose `cause` is the thrown value, and the caller still receives the original rejection unchanged ([validated by: called with session and error when stream fails](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L278), [validated by: wraps a rejected string in an Error with cause for onError while rethrowing the string unchanged](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L25), [validated by: wraps a rejected plain object in an Error with cause for onError while rethrowing the object unchanged](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L35), [validated by: wraps a rejected undefined in an Error with cause for onError while rethrowing undefined unchanged](../../src/orchestration/onErrorNonError.acceptance.test.ts#L59)).
 
